@startuml DB-PromotionPipeline-BuildMaster-ProGet
' ============================================================
' Diagram: Database Package Promotion Pipeline
' Purpose: Shows the BuildMaster pipeline stages that promote
'          ATAPUtilities.Database from Experimental through
'          Production, and the ProGet NuGet feeds used at
'          each stage gate.
' Author:  Generated for Sprint-0007
' ============================================================

skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowColor #444444
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7
skinparam NoteBorderColor #F9A825
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #888888
skinparam SequenceBoxBorderColor #888888

title "ATAPUtilities.Database — BuildMaster Promotion Pipeline\n(Experimental → Development → Integration → QA → Production)"

' -------------------------------------------------------
' Actors / participants
' -------------------------------------------------------
actor       "Developer"                   as dev
participant "Git / NBGV\n(version.json)"  as git
participant "BuildMaster\nTrigger"        as bmTrigger   #LightBlue
participant "BM Stage:\nExperimental"     as stageExp    #E3F2FD
participant "BM Stage:\nDevelopment"      as stageDev    #E8F5E9
participant "BM Stage:\nIntegration"      as stageInt    #FFF9C4
participant "BM Stage:\nQA"              as stageQA     #FCE4EC
participant "BM Stage:\nProduction"       as stageProd   #F3E5F5
database    "ProGet Feed:\nnuget-experimental"  as pgExp   #E3F2FD
database    "ProGet Feed:\nnuget-development"   as pgDev   #E8F5E9
database    "ProGet Feed:\nnuget-integration"   as pgInt   #FFF9C4
database    "ProGet Feed:\nnuget-qa"            as pgQA    #FCE4EC
database    "ProGet Feed:\nnuget-production"    as pgProd  #F3E5F5
collections "SQL Server\n(Experimental DB)"     as dbExp   #E3F2FD
collections "SQL Server\n(Development DB)"      as dbDev   #E8F5E9
collections "SQL Server\n(Integration DB)"      as dbInt   #FFF9C4
collections "SQL Server\n(QA DB)"              as dbQA    #FCE4EC
collections "SQL Server\n(Production DB)"       as dbProd  #F3E5F5

' -------------------------------------------------------
' Trigger: developer commits version.json height bump
' -------------------------------------------------------
dev       -> git       : git commit (version.json\nor any Database/** change)
git       -> bmTrigger : Webhook / Git trigger\n(branch: sprint worktree)
bmTrigger -> stageExp  : Start Experimental stage

' -------------------------------------------------------
' Stage 1: Experimental
' -------------------------------------------------------
note over stageExp
  **Experimental Stage**
  Pre-release suffix: -Sprint.{height}
  Runs on: developer workstation or CI agent
end note

stageExp -> stageExp   : 1. Resolve-FeedName\n   (Tier=Experimental, FeedType=nuget)
stageExp -> stageExp   : 2. New-DatabaseChangePackage\n   (pack + NBGV version resolution)
stageExp -> pgExp      : 3. Push ATAPUtilities.Database\n   <version>-Sprint.N.nupkg
stageExp -> stageExp   : 4. Invoke-Flyway.ps1\n   (target: Experimental DB\n    baseline or migrate)
stageExp -> dbExp      : 5. Flyway migrate\n   (V*.sql + R*.sql + *.csv seed data)
stageExp -> stageExp   : 6. Run smoke tests\n   (Pester: DbManifestSchema.Tests.ps1)
stageExp --> stageDev  : Gate: smoke tests pass\n→ promote to Development

' -------------------------------------------------------
' Stage 2: Development
' -------------------------------------------------------
note over stageDev
  **Development Stage**
  Package still carries pre-release suffix.
  Promoted from Experimental feed.
end note

stageDev -> pgExp      : 1. Download package from\n   nuget-experimental
stageDev -> pgDev      : 2. Move-ProGetPackage\n   → nuget-development
stageDev -> stageExp   : 3. Invoke-Flyway.ps1\n   (target: Development DB)
stageDev -> dbDev      : 4. Flyway migrate\n   (idempotent; V* checksums validated)
stageDev -> stageDev   : 5. Run unit tests\n   (Pester full test suite)
stageDev --> stageInt  : Gate: all tests pass\n→ promote to Integration

' -------------------------------------------------------
' Stage 3: Integration
' -------------------------------------------------------
note over stageInt
  **Integration Stage**
  Integration DB is seeded from Production backup
  at sprint start (see Export-ProductionDatabaseForSprintInit).
  Tests run against integrated multi-service schema.
end note

stageInt -> pgDev      : 1. Download package from\n   nuget-development
stageInt -> pgInt      : 2. Move-ProGetPackage\n   → nuget-integration
stageInt -> dbInt      : 3. Flyway migrate\n   (target: Integration DB)
stageInt -> stageInt   : 4. Run integration tests\n   (end-to-end, multi-service)
stageInt --> stageQA   : Gate: integration tests pass\n+ human review (optional)\n→ promote to QA

' -------------------------------------------------------
' Stage 4: QA
' -------------------------------------------------------
note over stageQA
  **QA Stage**
  QA DB is seeded from Production backup.
  HermeticFeed active: only nuget-qa visible.
  Requires manual QA sign-off gate.
end note

stageQA -> pgInt       : 1. Download package from\n   nuget-integration
stageQA -> pgQA        : 2. Move-ProGetPackage\n   → nuget-qa
stageQA -> dbQA        : 3. Flyway migrate\n   (target: QA DB)
stageQA -> stageQA     : 4. Automated QA regression suite
stageQA -> stageQA     : 5. **Manual QA gate**\n   (human sign-off required)
stageQA --> stageProd  : Gate: QA approved\n→ promote to Production

' -------------------------------------------------------
' Stage 5: Production
' -------------------------------------------------------
note over stageProd
  **Production Stage**
  Pre-release suffix stripped (stable SemVer).
  Applied to Production DB during maintenance window.
  Package version pinned; no further changes.
end note

stageProd -> pgQA      : 1. Download package from\n   nuget-qa
stageProd -> pgProd    : 2. Move-ProGetPackage\n   → nuget-production\n   (strip pre-release suffix\n    if not already stable)
stageProd -> stageProd : 3. Maintenance window opens
stageProd -> dbProd    : 4. Flyway migrate\n   (target: Production DB\n    — cleanDisabled=true enforced)
stageProd -> stageProd : 5. Post-deploy smoke test
stageProd -> git       : 6. Tag git commit\n   v<Major>.<Minor>.<Patch>
stageProd -> dev       : 7. Notify: deployment complete

' -------------------------------------------------------
' Notes
' -------------------------------------------------------
note over pgExp, pgDev
  Packages in Experimental and Development
  feeds carry the **pre-release** SemVer suffix
  (e.g., 0.1.250-Sprint.42).
  Only Production feed holds stable packages.
end note

note over stageInt, stageQA
  Both Integration and QA DBs are restored from
  the **Production backup** created by
  Export-ProductionDatabaseForSprintInit.ps1
  at the start of each sprint.
end note

@enduml
